---
import GraphDiagram from '@/components/GraphDiagram.astro';
import PropertyPackContents from '@/components/property-pack/PropertyPackContents.astro';
import PropertyPackDiagramLegend from '@/components/property-pack/PropertyPackDiagramLegend.astro';
import PropertyPackPage from '@/components/property-pack/PropertyPackPage.astro';
import {
  boundaryDiagram,
  candidateManifest,
  contexts,
  contextRoute,
  contextStats,
  counts,
} from '@/lib/property-pack-model.mjs';
---
<PropertyPackPage
  title="Property Pack ontology candidate"
  description="The machine-generated Property Pack ontology candidate: an accelerated, non-normative component of SPDTF 2.0 awaiting Technical Working Group determination."
>
  <h1>Property Pack ontology</h1>

  <p class="lead">
    The Property Pack is the standardised bundle of information needed to support a
    property transaction. This ontology candidate models that bundle as a defined part
    of SPDTF 2.0, spanning several semantic contexts rather than pretending it is one
    universal business domain.
  </p>

  <div class="callout callout--key">
    <p class="callout__label">Accelerated determination</p>
    <p>
      <strong>The Technical Working Group must determine this candidate by the end of
      September 2026.</strong> The current <code>{candidateManifest.candidate_version}</code>
      model remains <code>{candidateManifest.candidate_status}</code>. Later domain,
      scheme and Interoperability working-group review may propose controlled changes;
      none of those reviews or an external authority decision has yet occurred.
    </p>
  </div>

  <PropertyPackContents items={[
    { id: 'what-it-is', label: 'What a Property Pack is' },
    { id: 'headline-counts', label: 'Candidate at a glance' },
    { id: 'boundaries', label: 'Contextual boundaries' },
    { id: 'reference', label: 'Explore the reference' },
    { id: 'scope', label: 'Scope and authority' },
  ]} />

  <h2 id="what-it-is">What a Property Pack is</h2>
  <p>
    It is an exchange and delivery profile: a governed set of information that travels
    with a property transaction and draws on conveyancing, estate agency, finance,
    property-data services, property technology, surveying and shared identifiers. The
    451 required source items define the current coverage boundary; they do not prescribe
    451 RDF properties or reproduce the structure of a JSON document.
  </p>

  <h2 id="headline-counts">Candidate at a glance</h2>
  <div class="v2-metrics">
    <div class="v2-metric"><strong>{counts.sourceItems}</strong><span>required source data points, each traced to the candidate</span></div>
    <div class="v2-metric"><strong>{counts.resources}</strong><span>OWL resources: {counts.classes} classes and {counts.objectProperties + counts.datatypeProperties} properties</span></div>
    <div class="v2-metric"><strong>{counts.schemes}</strong><span>controlled-vocabulary schemes with {counts.concepts} curated concepts</span></div>
    <div class="v2-metric"><strong>{counts.shapes}</strong><span>SHACL node shapes carrying {counts.constraints} property constraints</span></div>
    <div class="v2-metric"><strong>{contexts.length}</strong><span>semantic homes: six bounded contexts, one common boundary and one scheme context</span></div>
    <div class="v2-metric"><strong>{counts.topicConcepts}</strong><span>source-topic concepts for consolidated Property Pack questions</span></div>
  </div>

  <h2 id="boundaries">Contextual boundaries</h2>
  <p>
    Every ontology resource has one semantic home. The dashed lines below mean only that
    each context interoperates through the Common boundary. They do not assert reviewed
    cross-domain mappings, control or inheritance. Cross-domain mappings remain
    <strong>awaiting working-group evidence</strong>.
  </p>
  <PropertyPackDiagramLegend variant="boundary" />
  <GraphDiagram
    source={boundaryDiagram()}
    minHeight="560px"
    caption="Declared context architecture: six bounded contexts, the DBT Smart Data scheme context, and the deliberately small Common boundary. Click a node to open its context page."
  />

  <div class="v2-card-grid">
    {contexts.map((context) => {
      const stats = contextStats(context.id);
      return (
        <a class="v2-card" href={contextRoute(context)}>
          <span class={`pill ${context.kind === 'common-boundary' ? 'pill--brand' : context.kind === 'scheme-context' ? 'pill--warn' : 'pill--info'}`}>
            {context.kind === 'bounded-context' ? 'Bounded context' : context.kind === 'common-boundary' ? 'Common boundary' : 'Scheme context'}
          </span>
          <h3>{context.label}</h3>
          <p>{context.definition}</p>
          <p class="v2-card__meta">{stats.resources} resources · {stats.sourceItems} source data points</p>
        </a>
      );
    })}
  </div>

  <h2 id="reference">Explore the reference</h2>
  <div class="v2-card-grid">
    <a class="v2-card" href="/spdtf-2/property-pack/definition-and-scope"><span class="pill pill--brand">451 items</span><h3>Definition and scope</h3><p>Inspect every required source item, constraint, semantic home, candidate disposition and evidence trace.</p></a>
    <a class="v2-card" href="/spdtf-2/property-pack/pdtf-1-lineage"><span class="pill pill--brand">Lineage</span><h3>PDTF 1.0 lineage</h3><p>Separate proven schema coverage from the incomplete semantic crosswalk to the ontology extracted from PDTF 1.0.</p></a>
    <a class="v2-card" href="/spdtf-2/property-pack/model"><span class="pill pill--brand">Atlas</span><h3>Complete model</h3><p>A class-relationship diagram in the PDTF 1.0 convention, with synchronized structured references for all 159 candidate resources.</p></a>
    <a class="v2-card" href="/spdtf-2/property-pack/resources"><span class="pill pill--info">OWL</span><h3>Ontology resources</h3><p>Human definitions, technical identifiers, semantic homes, domains, ranges, constraints and evidence traces.</p></a>
    <a class="v2-card" href="/spdtf-2/property-pack/data-dictionary"><span class="pill pill--info">451 items</span><h3>Data dictionary</h3><p>The exact Property Pack source scope, source constraints and candidate-model disposition for every item.</p></a>
    <a class="v2-card" href="/spdtf-2/property-pack/vocabularies"><span class="pill pill--info">SKOS</span><h3>Controlled vocabularies</h3><p>Fourteen curated value schemes plus the distinct source-topic concept layer.</p></a>
    <a class="v2-card" href="/spdtf-2/property-pack/shapes"><span class="pill pill--info">SHACL</span><h3>Validation shapes</h3><p>Forty-five target-class shapes and every emitted datatype, class, count and pattern constraint.</p></a>
    <a class="v2-card" href="/spdtf-2/property-pack/coverage"><span class="pill pill--success">Traceable</span><h3>Source coverage</h3><p>How all 451 source items reach candidate constructs without importing the legacy ontology.</p></a>
    <a class="v2-card" href="/spdtf-2/property-pack/standards"><span class="pill pill--warn">Exact claims</span><h3>Standards profile</h3><p>RDF 1.2 Basic, SPARQL 1.2 and SHACL 1.2 targets, with explicit non-claims.</p></a>
    <a class="v2-card" href="/spdtf-2/property-pack/validation"><span class="pill pill--success">Evidence</span><h3>Technical validation</h3><p>Parser, SHACL probe, competency-query and deterministic-regeneration results.</p></a>
    <a class="v2-card" href="/spdtf-2/property-pack/technical-working-group-determination"><span class="pill pill--warn">Pending</span><h3>Technical determination</h3><p>Review remit, deadline, evidence, questions and the decision record that must be completed before any determination is claimed.</p></a>
    <a class="v2-card" href="/spdtf-2/property-pack/review-and-releases"><span class="pill pill--info">Later</span><h3>Review and releases</h3><p>How later domain review, controlled change and immutable versions follow the accelerated technical determination.</p></a>
  </div>

  <h2 id="scope">Scope and authority</h2>
  <div class="v2-note-grid">
    <section>
      <h3>Closed business-data scope</h3>
      <p>Exactly the 451 workbook rows marked Required. Supporting ontology constructs make the data meaningful but do not enlarge that business-data scope.</p>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h3>Greenfield semantics</h3>
      <p>PDTF 1.0 contains the Property Pack source definition and its extracted ontology should contain corresponding meaning. This candidate imports neither topology; the item-level semantic crosswalk remains incomplete.</p>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h3>Human authority</h3>
      <p>AI drafted the candidate. The Technical Working Group makes the accelerated initial determination; later working groups may review and propose versioned changes. Government use does not itself grant OPDA external authority.</p>
    </section>
  </div>
</PropertyPackPage>
